    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0515" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">494.11 L 25/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Woods</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-21T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1924—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>105. Embassy’s number 60, April 1st, 2 p.m. You are authorized to accept $15,000
                    United States currency offered by Foreign Office in settlement of Langdon claim.
                    Endeavor effect prompt settlement. Telegraph when payment made.<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d326-f1"/></p>
                <p>You may explain to Foreign Office that offer is accepted because of willingness
                    of parents of Langdon that matter be settled in that manner.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d326-f1" n="80" xml:id="d326-f1-content">
                <p>The Chargé in Japan reported on July 5, 1924, that he had been handed on that
                    date, by the Foreign Office, a draft for $15,000 United States currency in
                    settlement of the Langdon claim (file no. 494.11 L 25/18).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
